            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Influence in Latin America</strong><br>\nHe supported leftist movements across Latin America and Africa, influencing global politics and fostering revolutionary movements worldwide.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years and Retirement</strong><br>\nCastro's health problems began to emerge in the public eye in 2006, leading him to officially retire in 2008, handing power to his brother, Raúl Castro.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nFidel Castro died in 2016, leaving behind a contentious legacy that includes both praise for social policies in Cuba and criticism for economic mismanagement and human rights violations.</p>\n"
              },
